    "The request has been fulfilled and resulted in a new resource being created.": "请求已完成，并创建了新资源。",
    "Then just send a request to the following URL, followed by the request path:": "然后向以下 URL 加上请求路径发送请求即可：",
    "Only members with the API Catalog Manager role can manage System Environments": "只有拥有 API 目录管理员角色的成员才能管理系统环境",
    "Please submit your request and a member of our team will be in touch shortly.": "请提交你的请求，我们团队的成员会尽快与你联系。",
    "The server successfully processed the request, but is not returning any content.": "服务器已成功处理请求，但不返回任何内容。",
    "Controls whether to send request information from the inline suggestion provider.": "控制是否从内联建议提供方发送请求信息。",
    "Try refreshing the page. If you keep getting this error, contact help@postman.com.": "请尝试刷新页面。如果持续出现此错误，请联系 help@postman.com。",
    "This and all future requests should be directed to the given URI.": "此请求及以后的所有请求都应定向到指定的 URI。",
    "Add a domain to allow cookies for that domain to be accessed in scripts. Learn more about": "添加域名以允许脚本访问该域名的 Cookie。了解更多：",
    "Just install a certificate to start routing HTTPS requests through Postman's proxy server.": "只需安装证书，即可开始通过 Postman 的代理服务器路由 HTTPS 请求。",
    "Includes collections, requests, folders linked to the update, notifying collection watchers.": "包含与该更新关联的集合、请求、文件夹，并通知集合关注者。",
    "This includes collections, requests, folders linked to the update, notifying collection watchers.": "这包括与该更新关联的集合、请求、文件夹，并通知集合关注者。",
    "Enter request paths for your API endpoints and then the expected response code and response body to create an": "输入 API 端点的请求路径，以及预期的响应码和响应正文，以创建",
    "The server successfully processed the request, but is returning information that may be from another source.": "服务器已成功处理请求，但返回的信息可能来自其他来源。",
    "You've successfully set instructions for the next billing cycle. Hold tight while we redirect you to Billing Overview": "你已成功设置下一个账单周期的指令。请稍候，正在跳转到账单概览",
    "Total number of users with requests sent vs. the number of users who faced authorization errors while using your APIs.": "已发送请求的用户总数，与使用你的 API 时遇到授权错误的用户数之比。",
    "This means the requester has asked the server to switch protocols and the server is acknowledging that it will do so.": "这表示请求方已要求服务器切换协议，服务器确认将执行切换。",
    "No AI request was found for the provided requestId and collectionId. Check them and try again or use an alternative block.": "未找到与所提供 requestId 和 collectionId 对应的 AI 请求。请检查后重试，或使用其他块。",
    "The server successfully processed the request, but is not returning any content. Unlike a 204 response, this response requires that the requester reset the document view.": "服务器已成功处理请求，但不返回任何内容。与 204 响应不同，此响应要求请求方重置文档视图。",
    "The server has fulfilled a GET request for the resource, and the response is a representation of the result of one or more instance-manipulations applied to the current instance.": "服务器已完成对该资源的 GET 请求，响应是对当前实例应用一个或多个实例操作后结果的表示。",
    "The request has been accepted for processing, but the processing has not been completed. The request might or might not eventually be acted upon, as it might be disallowed when processing actually takes place.": "请求已被接受处理，但处理尚未完成。该请求最终可能被执行，也可能不被执行，因为在实际处理时可能被拒绝。",
    "The response to the request can be found under another URI using a GET method. When received in response to a POST (or PUT/DELETE), it should be assumed that the server has received the data and the redirect should be issued with a separate GET message.": "请求的响应可通过 GET 方法在另一个 URI 下找到。当它作为对 POST（或 PUT/DELETE）的响应收到时，应认为服务器已接收数据，并应以单独的 GET 消息发起重定向。",
    "In this occasion, the request should be repeated with another URI, but future requests can still use the original URI. In contrast to 303, the request method should not be changed when reissuing the original request. For instance, a POST request must be repeated using another POST request.": "在这种情况下，应使用另一个 URI 重新发起请求，但以后的请求仍可使用原始 URI。与 303 不同，重新发起原始请求时不应更改请求方法。例如，POST 请求必须以另一个 POST 请求重新发起。",
    "Standard response for successful HTTP requests. The actual response will depend on the request method used. In a GET request, the response will contain an entity corresponding to the requested resource. In a POST request the response will contain an entity describing or containing the result of the action.": "HTTP 请求成功的标准响应。实际响应取决于所用的请求方法。在 GET 请求中，响应将包含与所请求资源对应的实体；在 POST 请求中，响应将包含描述或包含操作结果的实体。",
    "As a WebDAV request may contain many sub-requests involving file operations, it may take a long time to complete the request. This code indicates that the server has received and is processing the request, but no response is available yet. This prevents the client from timing out and assuming the request was lost.": "由于 WebDAV 请求可能包含许多涉及文件操作的子请求，完成请求可能耗时较长。此代码表示服务器已收到并正在处理请求，但暂无可用响应。这可防止客户端超时并误以为请求丢失。",
